WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.610
Primary Three needed times tables, seven

2
00:00:03.610 --> 00:00:06.050
of them, printed for every desk.

3
00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:09.380
Writing them out took me a whole evening.

4
00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:12.260
With Python, a loop writes a

5
00:00:12.260 --> 00:00:14.000
times table in three lines.

6
00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:17.840
Today: loops in Python, with

7
00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:19.640
for, range and while.

8
00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:22.720
A for loop runs the same

9
00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:24.800
lines once for each value.

10
00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:28.020
Here, n takes the values one to

11
00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:29.600
ten, one after another.

12
00:00:30.290 --> 00:00:32.650
Each time round, Python prints one

13
00:00:32.650 --> 00:00:34.250
line of the seven times table.

14
00:00:34.870 --> 00:00:37.290
The indented line is the body of the loop.

15
00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:40.980
range gives the numbers to loop over.

16
00:00:41.590 --> 00:00:44.630
range of one, eleven starts at one

17
00:00:44.630 --> 00:00:47.050
and stops just before eleven.

18
00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:49.200
So it gives one to ten.

19
00:00:49.960 --> 00:00:51.680
Stopping one early surprises

20
00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:53.920
everyone, so say it out loud.

21
00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:57.180
Loops can also add things up.

22
00:00:57.800 --> 00:01:00.400
Start a total at zero before the loop.

23
00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:04.020
Inside the loop, add each value to it.

24
00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:06.300
After the loop, print the total.

25
00:01:06.920 --> 00:01:09.580
This pattern, a running total, is in

26
00:01:09.580 --> 00:01:11.580
nearly every useful program.

27
00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:14.380
Sometimes you don’t know how

28
00:01:14.380 --> 00:01:15.580
many times to repeat.

29
00:01:16.370 --> 00:01:18.450
A while loop repeats as long as

30
00:01:18.450 --> 00:01:19.730
its condition is true.

31
00:01:20.290 --> 00:01:23.810
Here, the class saves fifty a week until

32
00:01:23.810 --> 00:01:25.610
it has four hundred for a football.

33
00:01:26.320 --> 00:01:27.740
If the condition never becomes

34
00:01:27.740 --> 00:01:30.100
false, the loop never ends.

35
00:01:31.430 --> 00:01:31.910
Quick check!

36
00:01:32.550 --> 00:01:35.750
A loop uses range of one, five.

37
00:01:36.370 --> 00:01:38.050
Which numbers does it give?

38
00:01:39.330 --> 00:01:42.610
One, two, three, four.

39
00:01:43.330 --> 00:01:46.150
Range stops just before the second number.

40
00:01:46.750 --> 00:01:50.010
To count to five, write range of one, six.

41
00:01:50.800 --> 00:01:53.040
This off-by-one mistake is so

42
00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:54.580
common it has a name.

43
00:01:55.860 --> 00:01:57.800
Loops do the boring work for you.

44
00:01:58.350 --> 00:02:00.350
Print a times table for any number.

45
00:02:01.040 --> 00:02:02.480
Add up a week of rainfall.

46
00:02:03.260 --> 00:02:04.720
Make a numbered list of

47
00:02:04.720 --> 00:02:06.140
forty seats for an exam.

48
00:02:06.880 --> 00:02:08.600
Count down the days to the end of term.

49
00:02:09.860 --> 00:02:10.600
One warning.

50
00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:13.580
If a while loop’s condition never becomes

51
00:02:13.580 --> 00:02:15.760
false, the program runs forever.

52
00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:19.300
On the phone, Darsi stops any program

53
00:02:19.300 --> 00:02:21.640
after three seconds, so nothing hangs.

54
00:02:22.360 --> 00:02:24.060
If that happens, check what

55
00:02:24.060 --> 00:02:25.680
changes inside the loop.

56
00:02:26.930 --> 00:02:29.050
In the app, open Step through a

57
00:02:29.050 --> 00:02:31.710
program and choose A loop that adds.

58
00:02:32.510 --> 00:02:35.150
Before each Next, say what

59
00:02:35.150 --> 00:02:36.190
total will become.

60
00:02:36.880 --> 00:02:40.080
Then change range of one, five to

61
00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:43.180
range of one, eleven, and jump to

62
00:02:43.180 --> 00:02:44.480
the end: fifty-five.

63
00:02:45.730 --> 00:02:46.230
Your turn.

64
00:02:46.840 --> 00:02:48.840
A loop prints one line for each

65
00:02:48.840 --> 00:02:50.940
value in range of zero, five.

66
00:02:51.500 --> 00:02:53.460
How many lines does it print?

67
00:02:54.770 --> 00:02:55.130
Five.

68
00:02:55.890 --> 00:02:58.550
Remember: for repeats the indented

69
00:02:58.550 --> 00:03:00.550
lines once for each value.

70
00:03:01.190 --> 00:03:03.750
range stops before its second number.

71
00:03:04.370 --> 00:03:06.050
A running total starts at

72
00:03:06.050 --> 00:03:07.550
zero before the loop.

73
00:03:08.170 --> 00:03:10.470
And while repeats until its

74
00:03:10.470 --> 00:03:11.590
condition is false.

75
00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:15.280
Try it in class tomorrow: Human loop.

76
00:03:15.920 --> 00:03:18.500
Write a for loop on the board, and let

77
00:03:18.500 --> 00:03:20.980
pupils be the computer: one pupil

78
00:03:20.980 --> 00:03:23.160
keeps the total on the board while the

79
00:03:23.160 --> 00:03:24.960
class reads out each value.

80
00:03:25.620 --> 00:03:27.880
Then change the range and run it again.
